# Launch assets (AS)

This is the short form. Before writing code in this area, read the full rules with reasons, bad/good examples and checks: `.ui-polish/rules/24-launch-assets.md`.

- **AS-01 Take an asset inventory and ask for what is missing** (error). During the brand intake (BR-02, BR-03), list each launch asset and whether the repository has it: logo (full and mark, light and dark), favicon (SVG plus 32px ICO), apple-touch-icon (180px PNG), manifest icons (192px and 512px), social preview image (1200×630), product screenshots or photography, and for marketing surfaces privacy and terms pages. Ask the owner for every missing item in one message, each with options: provide the file, let you generate a placeholder (from the logo or initials) marked "assumed", or skip with a reason. Record the answers in the Assets table of `design.md`.
- **AS-02 A complete icon set** (warning). A favicon alone is not enough. Ship an SVG favicon (it can switch colour with `prefers-color-scheme`), a 32px `favicon.ico` for old browsers and feed readers, a 180×180 PNG `apple-touch-icon` with a solid background (iOS ignores transparency and paints it black), and, for apps that can be installed or pinned, 192px and 512px icons in the web app manifest, including a maskable one. Generate them all from one square source mark so they match.
- **AS-03 Theme colour and manifest** (info). Set `<meta name="theme-color">` from the background token, once per colour scheme (`media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"` for the dark one), so mobile browser chrome matches the page. Ship a web app manifest (`site.webmanifest`, or `app/manifest.ts` in Next.js) with the product's `name`, `short_name`, `theme_color`, `background_color` and the icons from AS-02.
- **AS-04 Logos work on every background** (warning). Use the real logo files from the inventory (AS-01), never a text wordmark typed in the body font as a stand-in unless `design.md` says so. Provide a version for light and for dark surfaces (or an SVG using `currentColor`), keep its clear space and minimum size, use the mark alone where space is tight (collapsed sidebar, favicon, mobile header), and give it alt text with the product name. Customer and partner logos in a logo wall use one treatment (all monochrome or all original colours) at optically equal sizes.
- **AS-05 No placeholder or random images** (error). Never ship images from placeholder or random-image services (placehold.co, via.placeholder.com, picsum.photos, source.unsplash.com, placekitten, dummyimage.com, loremflickr and similar). Use the product's own screenshots, photography from the owner, or a licensed image chosen for the section and saved in the repository with dimensions and alt text (FD-04, AX-03). If no image exists yet, design the section without one, or show a neutral, on-brand empty frame and list the missing image in the asset inventory (AS-01).
